| :--- | :--- |
| raw shared correlations | [2, 5, 0, 2] |
| derivative of raw-output sum with respect to kernel | [4, 6, 3, 5] |
| ReLU then max-pool | [5] |

A one-cell shift across a stride-two boundary changes local maxima: [1, 0] -> [0, 1].
\image(figures/cnn_shared_kernel.svg)
// result_end
\caption(One kernel is reused at all four valid positions. The measured raw-output-sum gradient adds those spatial contributions.)
\alttext(Three native boxes show the three-by-three input, one diagonal two-by-two shared kernel and the actual two-by-two output. A footer gives the four kernel derivatives four, six, three and five.)

> The network and the position information its head retains

For NHWC input X and HWIO kernel W, stride-one valid cross-correlation is

$$
Z_{n,i,j,f}=b_f+\sum_{a,b,c}X_{n,i+a,j+b,c}W_{a,b,c,f}.
$$
\alttext(Every spatial output uses the same kernel coefficients for its input patch and output channel.)

A k×k convolution with C input and F output channels learns k²CF+F scalars,
independent of image height and width. Its kernel derivative sums upstream
errors times the corresponding input pixels over the batch and spatial sites.
For the error signal Δ at the raw convolution output, that shared derivative is

$$
\frac{\partial\mathcal L}{\partial W_{a,b,c,f}}
=\sum_{n,i,j}X_{n,i+a,j+b,c}\,\Delta_{n,i,j,f}.
$$
\alttext(The derivative of one shared kernel coefficient sums each corresponding input pixel times the convolution-output error over all examples and spatial uses.)

ReLU produces max(0,Z). Local p×p max-pooling with stride p reduces the map
while retaining a grid of spatial positions; flattening then gives the dense
head a separate input coordinate for every retained position.

Global max-pooling keeps one maximum per channel. Permuting the spatial sites
of a feature map cannot change these maxima, so any following deterministic
head sees the same vector. This is a property of the feature map, not every
finite image translation. Valid-convolution boundaries can change which patches
exist, noise changes the maps, and local strided pooling depends on grid phase.
The explicit one-cell shift above disproves the original claim that any shift
smaller than a local pool window must leave the pooled result unchanged.

The main bar model has eight valid 3×3 filters, ReLU, local 2×2 pooling,
flattening, a 32-unit ReLU hidden layer and two logits: 6,578 learned scalars.
The shifted-position comparison uses a 16-unit hidden layer in both CNNs,
giving 3,330 local-pooling or 258 global-pooling scalars. Its dense baseline
uses 32 hidden units over all 144 pixels, giving 4,706 scalars. All models
initialize convolution/hidden weights with He uniform, output weights with
Glorot uniform and biases with zero; these tensor initializations and explicit
fits are not numerical reproductions of the old constructor-trained wrapper.
The main CNN's 80 convolution scalars are a small part of its total: the
flatten-to-hidden layer alone learns 6,432. Its 6,578 scalars exceed the dense
baseline's 4,706. Sharing a small kernel does not guarantee a smaller complete
network when a position-sensitive dense head dominates the parameter count.

The executed diagrams below probe the exact four forward configurations.
They do not train or restore a checkpoint. Named stages retain all dependencies;
the forward also retains integer max-pool winners for attribution, separately
from learned weights. Flow glyphs use shared linear spatial/channel scales, excluding batch
size, with a one-pixel visibility floor. Labels rotate 90 degrees; wide diagrams
remain scrollable on the website. Parameter counts come from actual traced
leaves rather than labels copied onto a schematic.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/cnn_main_architecture.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  namespace n=dm::nn;namespace m=n::models;n::set_num_threads(2);
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");std::filesystem::create_directories("figures");
  const std::vector<std::string> files{"cnn_main_architecture.svg","cnn_local_architecture.svg","cnn_global_architecture.svg","cnn_dense_architecture.svg"};
  const std::vector<std::string> names{"Main local CNN: hidden 32","Shift local CNN: hidden 16","Shift global CNN: hidden 16","Flattened dense baseline"};
  std::print("| actual configuration | traced learned scalars | store learned scalars |\n| :--- | ---: | ---: |\n");
  for(const int variant:{1,2,3,0}) {
    n::ParameterStore p(1);m::SmallImageCnnConfig config;config.hidden=variant==0?32:16;config.global_pool=variant==2;
    n::Module model([&](const n::Tensor& image) {
      if(variant==3)return m::DenseImageBaseline(p,image);
      const auto out=m::SmallImageCnn(p,image,config);
      n::model_stage("Shared VALID 3x3",image,out.conv_pre);
      n::model_stage("ReLU",out.conv_pre,out.conv_relu);
      n::model_stage(config.global_pool?"Full-map max":"Local max 2x2",out.conv_relu,out.pooled);
      n::model_stage("Flatten pooled map",out.pooled,out.flat);
      n::model_stage("Dense hidden ReLU",out.flat,out.hidden);
      n::model_stage("Two raw logits",out.hidden,out.logits);
      return out.logits;
    },names[variant]);
    n::ModelPlotOptions options;options.title=names[variant];options.style=n::ModelPlotStyle::Flow;options.detail=n::ModelPlotDetail::Blocks;
    options.labels.type=n::ModelPlotLabel::Full;options.labels.size=13;options.labels.wrap=28;
    options.sizing.spatial_scale=n::ModelPlotScale::Linear;options.sizing.channel_scale=n::ModelPlotScale::Linear;options.sizing.minimum_extent=1;
    options.spacing.layer=48;options.spacing.lane=48;
    const auto picture=model.plot(n::zeros({1,12,12,1}),options);
    picture.save_svg("build/"+files[variant]);
    if(variant)std::filesystem::copy_file("build/"+files[variant],"figures/"+files[variant],std::filesystem::copy_options::overwrite_existing);
    std::print("| {} | {} | {} |\n",names[variant],picture.parameter_count(),p.count());
    if(picture.parameter_count()!=p.count())return 1;
  }
}
