> The original noisy bars and a held-out split

The native generator makes 600 square 12×12 images: 300 horizontal bars
(class 0) and 300 vertical bars (class 1), alternating in original row order.
Each thickness-two bar spans the full other axis. Its first row or column is
uniform over 0..10; independent Gaussian pixel noise has standard deviation
0.08 and intensities are clipped to [0,1]. A separately stored noiseless mask
retains the true object even when a noisy pixel crosses an intensity threshold.

Seed 20240815, per-image normal-distribution construction, draw order and the
post-generation shuffle preserve the original report's data stream on this
standard-library implementation. Distribution/shuffle mappings need not be
bitwise identical across standard libraries. The first 420 shuffled rows are
fitting data and the remaining 180 are held out. This split does not select
hyperparameters or an epoch. Original row ids remain available for inspection.
The generator's double-valued draws are stored as Float32 tensor pixels; all
fits use Float32 parameters and computation. The earlier hand check uses Float64.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/cnn_bar_inputs.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  namespace n=dm::nn;
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  const auto data=n::make_bar_images(300);
  const std::vector<std::int64_t> fit(data.shuffled_rows.begin(),data.shuffled_rows.begin()+420),
      test(data.shuffled_rows.begin()+420,data.shuffled_rows.end());
  std::print("| partition | observations | horizontal | vertical |\n| :--- | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
  for(int part=0;part<2;++part) {
    const auto& rows=part?test:fit;const auto y=n::take_rows(data.labels,rows);
    const auto horizontal=n::sum(n::cast(n::equal(y,0),n::DType::Int64)).item();
    std::print("| {} | {} | {:.0f} | {:.0f} |\n",part?"held out":"fitting",rows.size(),horizontal,rows.size()-horizontal);
  }
  const auto classes=data.labels.to_vector<std::int64_t>();
  std::vector<std::int64_t> selected;std::vector<std::string> labels;
  for(int part=0;part<2;++part)for(int i=0;i<4;++i) {
    const auto row=(part?test:fit)[i];selected.push_back(row);
    labels.push_back(std::format("{} #{} {}",part?"test":"fit",row,classes[row]?"V":"H"));
  }
  auto picture=n::diagram_tensor_images(n::take_rows(data.images,selected),4,labels);
  picture.text({27,4},"Fitting inputs above, held-out inputs below",21)
         .save_svg("build/cnn_bar_inputs.svg");
  std::print("\nActual image tensor {}; true object pixels per image: {}.\n",data.images.shape(),n::sum(n::take_rows(data.object_mask,{0}),{1,2,3}).item());
}
