> Softmax, cross-entropy and an explicit tensor fit

For logits s and true class y, stable softmax cross-entropy is

$$
\ell(s,y)=\log\sum_c\exp(s_c)-s_y,\qquad
\frac{\partial\mathcal L}{\partial s_{n,c}}
=\frac{p_{n,c}-\mathbf1[c=y_n]}{B}
$$
\alttext(Cross-entropy is log-sum-exp of the logits minus the true-class logit. Its mean-minibatch score derivative is softmax probability minus the true one-hot label, divided by batch size.)

The native fused loss evaluates the log-sum-exp stably. Autodiff propagates this
error through both dense maps, ReLU, the actual maximum-pool winners and the
shared convolution. At a kernel offset, contributions from every application
are added. The earlier raw-correlation example isolates that sharing; a full
loss also includes all subsequent nonlinear and pooling derivatives.

The program below creates all six learned leaves before constructing the
optimizer, then visibly performs every SGD update. Learning rate is 0.05,
model/batch-order seeds are one, minibatch size is 16, and the epoch count is
fixed at 40. There is no L2 penalty, augmentation or early stopping. Initial
and final parameters are saved for the following filter and attribution checks.

The plotted loss is the sample-weighted mean of actual preupdate minibatch
losses during each epoch. Because parameters change between batches, this is
not a final fixed-model whole-dataset loss. Test data are evaluated after the
last update. The confusion matrix uses actual predictions, with true classes
in rows and predicted classes in columns.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/cnn_loss.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  namespace n=dm::nn;namespace m=n::models;n::set_num_threads(2);
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");std::filesystem::create_directories("figures");
  const auto data=n::make_bar_images(300);
  const std::vector<std::int64_t> fit(data.shuffled_rows.begin(),data.shuffled_rows.begin()+420),
      test(data.shuffled_rows.begin()+420,data.shuffled_rows.end());
  const auto fit_x=n::take_rows(data.images,fit),fit_y=n::take_rows(data.labels,fit),
      test_x=n::take_rows(data.images,test),test_y=n::take_rows(data.labels,test);
  n::ParameterStore p(1);m::SmallImageCnnConfig config;
  { n::NoGradGuard guard;(void)m::SmallImageCnn(p,n::take_rows(fit_x,{0}),config); }
  p.save("build/cnn_initial.npz");
  n::OptimizerConfig rule;rule.kind=n::OptimizerKind::Sgd;
  n::Optimizer optimizer(p,.05,rule);n::BatchOrder batches(fit.size(),16,1);
  std::vector<double> epoch,mean_nll;std::size_t updates=0;
  std::print("| epoch | sample-weighted preupdate minibatch NLL |\n| ---: | ---: |\n");
  for(int e=0;e<40;++e) {
    batches.begin_epoch();n::WeightedMean average;
    for(auto rows=batches.next();!rows.empty();rows=batches.next()) {
      const auto logits=m::SmallImageCnn(p,n::take_rows(fit_x,rows),config).logits;
      const auto loss=n::sparse_softmax_cross_entropy(logits,n::take_rows(fit_y,rows));
      optimizer.minimize(loss);++updates;average.add(loss.item(),rows.size());
    }
    epoch.push_back(e+1);mean_nll.push_back(average.value());
    if(e==0 || (e+1)%10==0)std::print("| {} | {:.9f} |\n",e+1,average.value());
  }
  p.save("build/cnn_bars.npz");
  n::NoGradGuard guard;
  const auto scores=m::SmallImageCnn(p,test_x,config).logits;
  n::ConfusionMatrix confusion(2);confusion.add(test_y,n::argmax(scores,1));
  n::ConfusionMatrixPlotOptions matrix;matrix.labels={"horizontal","vertical"};matrix.title="Held-out noisy bars: actual predictions";
  confusion.save_svg("build/cnn_bars_confusion.svg",matrix);
  std::filesystem::copy_file("build/cnn_bars_confusion.svg","figures/cnn_bars_confusion.svg",std::filesystem::copy_options::overwrite_existing);
  std::print("\nLearned scalars {}; learned leaves {}; actual optimizer calls {}.\nFitting accuracy {:.6f}; held-out accuracy {:.6f}; held-out NLL {:.9f}.\n",p.count(),p.parameters().size(),updates,n::accuracy(m::SmallImageCnn(p,fit_x,config).logits,fit_y),confusion.accuracy(),n::sparse_softmax_cross_entropy(scores,test_y).item());
  auto plot=dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
  plot.line(epoch,mean_nll,"batch loss",{37,99,235},2).legend({"SGD batch mean"},{{37,99,235}})
      .title("Actual sample-weighted minibatch loss by epoch")
      .x_label("completed epoch").y_label("mean cross-entropy")
      .x_limits(1,40).y_limits(0,.45).save_svg("build/cnn_loss.svg");
}
