> Signed relevance redistribution and an initialized-weight control

For finite nonnegative activations a, let W⁺=max(W,0). A stabilized dense
z-plus redistribution of incoming relevance R is

$$
R_{in}=a\odot\left[\left(R\oslash(aW^++\varepsilon)\right)(W^+)^T\right].
$$
\alttext(Each incoming score is divided by its sum of positive activation-weight contributions plus epsilon, then distributed back through those positive connections and multiplied by the input activations.)

The convolutional version uses the same positive kernel and its input adjoint:

$$
R_{image}=X\odot\mathrm{ConvInputAdjoint}
\left(W^+, R_{map}\oslash(\mathrm{Conv}(X,W^+)+\varepsilon)\right).
$$
\alttext(Convolution relevance is divided by positive forward contributions plus epsilon and redistributed by the matching convolution input adjoint.)

The native explanation seeds the selected raw logit, including output bias,
then redistributes through positive output, hidden and convolution connections.
Denominators omit biases and negative weights. The actual recorded max-pool
argmax scatters relevance back to the feature map; ties use the first maximum.
ReLU is passed through using its nonnegative forward activations. Epsilon is
1e−9 here. No fit or gradient update occurs during this inspection.

This is a custom stabilized signed-logit adaptation of positive-connection LRP.
A negative selected logit can give negative maps. Epsilon, zero positive paths
and floating arithmetic mean relevance need not be exactly conserved. Bias
credit is not assigned to a separate bias node. These maps are not ordinary
input gradients, class probabilities, counterfactual effects or causal proofs.
The table therefore reports actual selected scores, retained signed sums and
residuals instead of assuming a conservation identity.

We select two held-out images per true class and compare trained weights with
the saved initialized weights at exactly the same target classes. The mask
fraction is sum(|R|×true mask)/sum(|R|); if absolute mass is zero it is missing
(nan), not replaced by an invented floor. Bright input pixels enter the rule
multiplicatively, so substantial concentration on the bar can occur before
learning. The initialized-weight control tests that alternative explanation.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/cnn_relevance.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  namespace n=dm::nn;namespace m=n::models;n::set_num_threads(2);
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");std::filesystem::create_directories("figures");
  n::NoGradGuard guard;const auto data=n::make_bar_images(300);
  const auto truth=data.labels.to_vector<std::int64_t>();std::vector<std::int64_t> rows;
  for(int category=0;category<2;++category) {
    int count=0;
    for(std::size_t i=420;i<data.shuffled_rows.size() && count<2;++i) {
      const auto row=data.shuffled_rows[i];if(truth[row]==category){rows.push_back(row);++count;}
    }
  }
  const auto input=n::take_rows(data.images,rows),mask=n::take_rows(data.object_mask,rows);
  n::ParameterStore trained(1),initial(1);
  (void)m::SmallImageCnn(trained,input);(void)m::SmallImageCnn(initial,input);
  trained.load("build/cnn_bars.npz");initial.load("build/cnn_initial.npz");
  const auto explanation=m::SmallImageCnnZPlus(trained,input);
  const auto targets=explanation.target_ids.to_vector<std::int64_t>();
  const auto control=m::SmallImageCnnZPlus(initial,input,targets);
  const auto mass=n::sum(n::abs(explanation.input_relevance),{1,2,3}),
      control_mass=n::sum(n::abs(control.input_relevance),{1,2,3});
  const auto share=n::where(n::greater(mass,0),n::sum(n::abs(explanation.input_relevance)*mask,{1,2,3})/mass,std::numeric_limits<double>::quiet_NaN()).to_vector<float>();
  const auto control_share=n::where(n::greater(control_mass,0),n::sum(n::abs(control.input_relevance)*mask,{1,2,3})/control_mass,std::numeric_limits<double>::quiet_NaN()).to_vector<float>();
  const auto seed=n::sum(explanation.output_relevance,{1}).to_vector<float>(),retained=n::sum(explanation.input_relevance,{1,2,3}).to_vector<float>();
  std::print("| original row | truth | fixed target | trained absolute mass on true bar | initial same-target fraction | selected logit | retained signed sum | score minus retained sum |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
  for(std::size_t i=0;i<rows.size();++i)std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {:.6f} | {:.6f} | {:.8f} | {:.8f} | {:.3e} |\n",rows[i],truth[rows[i]],targets[i],share[i],control_share[i],seed[i],retained[i],seed[i]-retained[i]);
  const auto one=n::take_rows(input,{0});const auto horizontal=m::SmallImageCnnZPlus(trained,one,{0}),vertical=m::SmallImageCnnZPlus(trained,one,{1});
  double contrast_scale=std::max(n::max(n::abs(horizontal.input_relevance)).item(),n::max(n::abs(vertical.input_relevance)).item());if(contrast_scale==0)contrast_scale=1;
  const auto contrast=n::concat({one,.5+horizontal.input_relevance/(2*contrast_scale),.5+vertical.input_relevance/(2*contrast_scale)},0);
  auto contrast_picture=n::diagram_tensor_images(contrast,3,{"input H","target H","target V"});
  contrast_picture.text({20,4},"Signed class contrasts: one symmetric score scale",19)
                  .save_svg("build/cnn_relevance_contrast.svg");
  std::filesystem::copy_file("build/cnn_relevance_contrast.svg","figures/cnn_relevance_contrast.svg",std::filesystem::copy_options::overwrite_existing);
  std::print("\nContrast target H: raw score {:.8f}, signed pixel sum {:.8f}; target V: raw score {:.8f}, signed pixel sum {:.8f}.\n",n::sum(horizontal.output_relevance).item(),n::sum(horizontal.input_relevance).item(),n::sum(vertical.output_relevance).item(),n::sum(vertical.input_relevance).item());
  double scale=std::max(n::max(n::abs(explanation.input_relevance)).item(),n::max(n::abs(control.input_relevance)).item());if(scale==0)scale=1;
  const auto panels=n::concat({input,.5+explanation.input_relevance/(2*scale),.5+control.input_relevance/(2*scale)},0);
  std::vector<std::string> labels;
  for(auto row:rows)labels.push_back(std::format("input #{} {}",row,truth[row]?"V":"H"));
  for(auto target:targets)labels.push_back(std::format("trained target {}",target));
  for(auto target:targets)labels.push_back(std::format("initial target {}",target));
  auto picture=n::diagram_tensor_images(panels,4,labels);
  picture.text({27,4},"Inputs, trained relevance, initialized same-target control",19)
         .save_svg("build/cnn_relevance.svg");
  std::print("Shared map scale [-M,+M], M={:.9f}; zero maps are mid-grey.\n",scale);
}
```
