| dense baseline | 4706 | 200 | 6400 | 1.000000 | 0.000000 | 4.392644882 |
| global CNN | 258 | 40 | 1280 | 1.000000 | 0.846000 | 0.316169739 |
\image(figures/cnn_shift_global_confusion.svg)
// result_end
\caption(The globally pooled model's actual shifted-position confusion. All 500 predictions are counted.)
\alttext(Two-class confusion for the global-pooling CNN under the early-to-late positional shift.)

\image(figures/cnn_shift_local_confusion.svg)
\caption(The local CNN fits early positions yet fails on the late-position split in this run.)
\alttext(Local CNN shifted-position confusion with observations on the wrong-class off-diagonal.)

\image(figures/cnn_shift_dense_confusion.svg)
\caption(The dense baseline's additional epochs fit training data but do not transfer to late positions here.)
\alttext(Dense baseline shifted-position confusion with observations on the wrong-class off-diagonal.)

On this fixed run, all three fitting accuracies are one. Global pooling reaches
84.6% on the shifted test; local pooling and the dense head reach zero. That
ranking supports the value of discarding position for this generated task. It
is not a guarantee for other seeds, image transformations or tasks where
spatial arrangement contains the label. It also does not make global pooling
perfectly invariant to the finite noisy image transformations used here.

> Original MNIST digits with verified native acquisition

The final experiment uses original 28×28 MNIST grayscale digits. Native
fetch obtains the standard files; fetch_file verifies the four compressed
resources against their published MD5 pins, including cached sources. The
program then reads those exact verified gzip IDX files through native read_idx,
casts pixels to Float32 and divides original bytes by 255. It does not trust
an unrelated unverified plain-file cache in place of those verified sources.
The resource names and digests agree with the official torchvision MNIST
source definitions; torchvision is a provenance reference, not an execution
dependency. No Python data-preparation step is involved.

Training uses original training-file rows 0..511, validation uses training rows
512..639, and final evaluation uses official-test rows 0..255. Those small
fixed prefixes are disjoint by source and role but are not representative
full-dataset benchmark samples. The model is the same default eight-filter
local CNN with ten output logits, now learning 43,706 scalars because the
26×26 convolution map yields a larger flattened head. Six epochs of Adam
at 0.001 and batch size 32 give 96 explicit updates. Model and batch-order
seeds are eleven. The lowest validation cross-entropy selects a checkpoint;
o official-test score participates in selection.

The executed architecture and actual source-image preview are saved alongside
the loss and test confusion. This example's digit accuracy is an illustrative
small-prefix result, not a claim about the usual full MNIST benchmark.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/cnn_mnist_loss.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  namespace n=dm::nn;namespace m=n::models;n::set_num_threads(2);
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");std::filesystem::create_directories("figures");
  const auto directory=std::filesystem::path(dm::datasets::fetch("mnist"));
  const std::vector<std::pair<std::string,std::string>> sources{
    {"train-images-idx3-ubyte.gz","f68b3c2dcbeaaa9fbdd348bbdeb94873"},
    {"train-labels-idx1-ubyte.gz","d53e105ee54ea40749a09fcbcd1e9432"},
    {"t10k-images-idx3-ubyte.gz","9fb629c4189551a2d022fa330f9573f3"},
    {"t10k-labels-idx1-ubyte.gz","ec29112dd5afa0611ce80d1b7f02629c"}};
  std::print("| verified compressed source | MD5 |\n| :--- | :--- |\n");
  for(const auto& [file,digest]:sources) {
    dm::datasets::fetch_file("https://ossci-datasets.s3.amazonaws.com/mnist/"+file,(directory/file).string(),digest,0,"mnist");
    std::print("| {} | {} |\n",file,digest);
  }
  const auto training_x=n::reshape(n::cast(n::read_idx((directory/"train-images-idx3-ubyte.gz").string()),n::DType::Float32),{60000,28,28,1})/255.;
  const auto training_y=n::cast(n::read_idx((directory/"train-labels-idx1-ubyte.gz").string()),n::DType::Int64);
  const auto official_x=n::reshape(n::cast(n::read_idx((directory/"t10k-images-idx3-ubyte.gz").string()),n::DType::Float32),{10000,28,28,1})/255.;
  const auto official_y=n::cast(n::read_idx((directory/"t10k-labels-idx1-ubyte.gz").string()),n::DType::Int64);
  const auto fit_x=n::slice_axis(training_x,0,0,512),fit_y=n::slice_axis(training_y,0,0,512),
      validation_x=n::slice_axis(training_x,0,512,640),validation_y=n::slice_axis(training_y,0,512,640),
      test_x=n::slice_axis(official_x,0,0,256),test_y=n::slice_axis(official_y,0,0,256);
  m::SmallImageCnnConfig config;config.classes=10;n::ParameterStore p(11);
  n::Module model([&](const n::Tensor& image) {
    const auto out=m::SmallImageCnn(p,image,config);
    n::model_stage("Shared VALID 3x3",image,out.conv_pre);
    n::model_stage("ReLU",out.conv_pre,out.conv_relu);
    n::model_stage("Local max 2x2",out.conv_relu,out.pooled);
    n::model_stage("Flatten pooled map",out.pooled,out.flat);
    n::model_stage("Dense 32 ReLU",out.flat,out.hidden);
    n::model_stage("Ten digit logits",out.hidden,out.logits);return out.logits;
  },"Executed small MNIST CNN");
  n::ModelPlotOptions architecture;architecture.title="Small MNIST CNN: actual 28x28 forward";
  architecture.labels.type=n::ModelPlotLabel::Full;architecture.labels.wrap=28;architecture.sizing.minimum_extent=1;
  const auto picture=model.plot(n::zeros({1,28,28,1}),architecture);
  picture.save_svg("build/cnn_mnist_architecture.svg");
  std::filesystem::copy_file("build/cnn_mnist_architecture.svg","figures/cnn_mnist_architecture.svg",std::filesystem::copy_options::overwrite_existing);
  if(picture.parameter_count()!=43706 || p.count()!=43706)return 1;
  n::OptimizerConfig rule;rule.kind=n::OptimizerKind::Adam;
  n::Optimizer optimizer(p,.001,rule);n::BatchOrder batches(512,32,11);
  double best=std::numeric_limits<double>::infinity();int best_epoch=0;std::size_t updates=0;
  std::vector<double> epoch,training_nll,validation_nll;
  std::print("\n| epoch | training preupdate batch NLL | validation NLL | validation accuracy |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
  for(int e=0;e<6;++e) {
    batches.begin_epoch();n::WeightedMean average;
    for(auto rows=batches.next();!rows.empty();rows=batches.next()) {
      const auto loss=n::sparse_softmax_cross_entropy(m::SmallImageCnn(p,n::take_rows(fit_x,rows),config).logits,n::take_rows(fit_y,rows));
      optimizer.minimize(loss);++updates;average.add(loss.item(),rows.size());
    }
    n::NoGradGuard guard;const auto scores=m::SmallImageCnn(p,validation_x,config).logits;
    const double value=n::sparse_softmax_cross_entropy(scores,validation_y).item();
    epoch.push_back(e+1);training_nll.push_back(average.value());validation_nll.push_back(value);
    std::print("| {} | {:.6f} | {:.6f} | {:.6f} |\n",e+1,average.value(),value,n::accuracy(scores,validation_y));
    if(value<best){best=value;best_epoch=e+1;p.save("build/cnn_mnist_best.npz");}
  }
  p.load("build/cnn_mnist_best.npz");n::NoGradGuard guard;
  const auto test_scores=m::SmallImageCnn(p,test_x,config).logits;
  n::ConfusionMatrix confusion(10);confusion.add(test_y,n::argmax(test_scores,1));
  n::ConfusionMatrixPlotOptions matrix;matrix.title="MNIST: actual official-test rows 0..255";
  confusion.save_svg("build/cnn_mnist_confusion.svg",matrix);
  std::filesystem::copy_file("build/cnn_mnist_confusion.svg","figures/cnn_mnist_confusion.svg",std::filesystem::copy_options::overwrite_existing);
  const auto digit_labels=n::slice_axis(test_y,0,0,10).to_vector<std::int64_t>();std::vector<std::string> labels;
  for(int i=0;i<10;++i)labels.push_back(std::format("test #{} true {}",i,digit_labels[i]));
  auto samples=n::diagram_tensor_images(n::slice_axis(test_x,0,0,10),5,labels,0,1,6);
  samples.text({74,4},"Original official-test images: source rows 0..9",20).save_svg("build/cnn_mnist_inputs.svg");
  std::filesystem::copy_file("build/cnn_mnist_inputs.svg","figures/cnn_mnist_inputs.svg",std::filesystem::copy_options::overwrite_existing);
  std::print("\nLearned scalars {}; actual Adam calls {}; selected epoch {}.\nOfficial-test prefix size {}; accuracy {:.6f}; NLL {:.9f}.\n",p.count(),updates,best_epoch,test_y.numel(),confusion.accuracy(),n::sparse_softmax_cross_entropy(test_scores,test_y).item());
  auto plot=dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
  plot.line(epoch,training_nll,"train",{37,99,235},2).line(epoch,validation_nll,"validation",{234,88,12},2)
      .legend({"train batches","validation"},{{37,99,235},{234,88,12}})
      .title("Small MNIST fit and held-out validation loss")
      .x_label("completed epoch").y_label("mean cross-entropy")
      .x_limits(1,6).y_limits(0,2.1).save_svg("build/cnn_mnist_loss.svg");
}
